{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QouCanonicalAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QouCanonicalAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qou_canonical_action_unique_up_to_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qou_canonical_action_unique_up_to_scalar","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-canonical-action.lean#L58-L110","doc":"**Uniqueness up to scalar** (conditional conjecture, named not asserted).\n\nThe canonical action is conjectured to be unique up to rescaling of\nthe Frobenius form: replacing `∫_A` by `λ·∫_A` sends `S_q ↦ λ·S_q`,\nso two canonical actions on the same Frobenius–Hopf data differ only\nby a single scalar `λ ∈ R×`.  Concretely, the gravity/gauge/matter\naction-term morphisms of `ca₂` are obtained from those of `ca₁` by a\ncommon automorphism `s : 𝟙_C ≅ 𝟙_C` of the monoidal unit (the\ncategorical avatar of multiplication by `λ`), applied uniformly to\nall three terms.\n\nThis is an irreducibly categorical claim over the opaque\n`QOUCanonicalAction` data — there is no scalar action on the abstract\nhom-spaces `𝟙_C ⟶ 𝟙_C` without further (`Preadditive` / `Linear`)\nstructure, so per the playbook fallback it is *named* as a `Prop`\nrather than given a vacuous proof.  An inhabitant (an instance of\n`QOUCanonicalActionUniqueUpToScalar`) is the open conjecture; its\nabsence is the honest open state.\n\nFull proof would require showing the evaluation/coevaluation maps are\ndetermined up to unique isomorphism by the duality data.\n\n**Composition side, 2026-09-15 (`qou-h0ou`).**  `s` was applied by\n*pre*-composition (`s.hom ≫ ca₁.action.gravity`).  That stopped\ntypechecking when `CategoricalAction.gravity` was retyped to the rank-2\npairing space `fh.obj ⊗ fh.obj ⟶ 𝟙_ C`: `s.hom` ends at `𝟙_ C`, which is\nno longer where `gravity` begins.\n\nIt is now applied by *post*-composition, uniformly to all three terms.\nThat is the side this docstring's own account of the rescaling asks for:\nthe claim is that replacing `∫_A` by `λ·∫_A` sends `S_q ↦ λ·S_q`, and the\nFrobenius form is the **last** map into the unit in each term, so\nrescaling it composes on the right.  The uniformity the paragraph above\npromises (\"applied uniformly to all three terms\") is preserved — for the\ntwo terms that are already endomorphisms of `𝟙_ C` the two sides agree in\nany case, since `End(𝟙_C)` is commutative in a monoidal category, though\nnothing here needs or asserts that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QOUCanonicalAction.action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QOUCanonicalAction.action","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-canonical-action.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The underlying categorical action, carrying the gravity, gauge,\nand matter term morphisms `tr(q·R_∫)`, `∫_A∘tr_A(F∧_q⋆_qF)`, and\n`∫_A(ψ*·𝒟_∇ψ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QOUCanonicalAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QOUCanonicalAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-canonical-action.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QOUCanonicalAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QOUCanonicalAction","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-canonical-action.lean#L32-L49","doc":"**Canonical action of a QOU.**\n\nGiven a QOU with connection, the categorical action\nS_q = tr(ℒ_q) decomposes into three terms:\n  S_q[∇, ∫_A, ψ] = tr(q · R_∫)           (gravity)\n                   + ∫_A ∘ tr_A(F_∇ ∧_q ⋆_q F_∇)  (gauge)\n                   + ∫_A(ψ* · 𝒟_∇ ψ)      (matter)\n\nThe action is unique up to rescaling of the Frobenius form ∫_A. ","signatureChunk":0}]}